        "passed": false,
        "score": 0.6,
        "rationale": "The agent correctly identified via wo.list_workorders that no work order on Transformer 1 had been closed (all three are APPR/WAPPR), correctly took the 'no closed work order' branch (used all four samples in the window, gave no verdict on a fix, created no work order), pulled the right gases for the right asset/site/window via iot.history, and produced a defensible IEC 60599 classification (T2 thermal) for the latest sample. It was also honest about tool failures rather than fabricating results",
        "details": {
          "task_completion": false,
          "data_retrieval_accuracy": true,
          "generalized_result_verification": false,
          "agent_sequence_correct": true,
          "clarity_and_justification": true,
          "hallucinations": false,
          "suggestions": "The agent correctly identified via wo.list_workorders that no work order on Transformer 1 had been closed (all three are APPR/WAPPR), correctly took the 'no closed work order' branch (used all four samples in the window, gave no verdict on a fix, created no work order), pulled the right gases for the right asset/site/window via iot.history, and produced a defensible IEC 60599 classification (T2 thermal) for the latest sample. It was also honest about tool failures rather than fabricating results. However, the task required an anomaly screen of hydrogen, acetylene and CO with a proper detector, and this was never delivered; the agent should have retried tsfm.find_models with task_id='tsfm_anomaly_detection' (its claim that the catalog has no anomaly models suggests a wrong query), persisted the retrieved samples to a data file in the working directory itself so tsfm.run_recipe could be executed, and retried fmsr.interpret_dga rather than settling on a manual ratio computation. It also skipped the iot.stream_extent confirmation step. The final answer therefore only partially satisfies the expected output (classification present, anomaly result missing)."
        }
